<subsection xml:id="quickreference-identity-rules">
<title>Identity Rules</title>
<p>(chapter <xref ref="ch-identity" text="global"/>)</p>
<p>If names <m>\script{a}</m> and <m>\script{b}</m> are identified on a branch, then, for any sentence <m>\metaA{}</m> in the branch, you may add <m>\metaA{}\substitute{\script{a}}{\script{b}}</m> to the branch.</p>
<p>A branch closes if and only if either (i) it contains some sentence <m>\metaA{}</m> along with its negation, <m>\enot\metaA{}</m>, or (ii) it contains, for some name <m>\script{a}</m>, the sentence <m>\script{a}{\neq}\script{a}</m>.</p>
<p>A branch is <term>complete</term> if and only if either (i) it is closed, or (ii) all of the following conditions are met:</p>
<p>
<ol>
<li>Every resolvable sentence in the branch has been resolved;</li>
<li>For every general quantified sentence <m>\metaA{}</m> in the branch, at least one instance of <m>\metaA{}</m> is in the branch; and, for every name <m>\script{a}</m> in the branch, the <m>\script{a}</m> instance of <m>\metaA{}</m> is in the branch; and</li>
<li>It is possible to select one name as the representative of each identity group in the branch such that, for every atomic sentence or negated atomic sentence in the branch other than a positive identity claim, its representative version is also in the branch.</li></ol></p></subsection>
</section>
<section xml:id="quickreference-natural-deduction-rules">
<title>Natural Deduction Rules</title>
<subsection xml:id="nd-proofrules">
<title>Basic Rules</title>
<p><alert>Conjunction Introduction</alert></p>
<image width="35%"><latex-image label="proof-0f6400cab3">
$\begin{nd}
	\have[m]{a}{\metaA{}}
	\have[n]{b}{\metaB{}}
	\have[\ ]{c}{\metaA{}\eand\metaB{}} \ai{a, b}
\end{nd}$
</latex-image>
<shortdescription>Natural deduction proof</shortdescription></image>
<p><alert>Conjunction Elimination</alert></p>
<image width="33%"><latex-image label="proof-cd45fcbf68">
$\begin{nd}
	\have[m]{ab}{\metaA{}\eand\metaB{}}
	\have[\ ]{a}{\metaA{}} \ae{ab}
	\have[\ ]{b}{\metaB{}} \ae{ab}
\end{nd}$
</latex-image>
<shortdescription>Natural deduction proof</shortdescription></image>
<p><alert>Disjunction Introduction</alert></p>
<image width="31%"><latex-image label="proof-384c0f62e8">
$\begin{nd}
	\have[m]{a}{\metaA{}}
	\have[\ ]{ab}{\metaA{}\eor\metaB{}}\oi{a}
	\have[\ ]{ba}{\metaB{}\eor\metaA{}}\oi{a}
\end{nd}$
</latex-image>
<shortdescription>Natural deduction proof</shortdescription></image>
<p><alert>Disjunction Elimination</alert></p>
<image width="36%"><latex-image label="proof-35269d6500">
$\begin{nd}
	\have[m]{ab}{\metaA{}\eor\metaB{}}
	\have[n]{nb}{\enot\metaB{}}
	\have[\ ]{a}{\metaA{}} \oe{ab,nb}
\end{nd}$
</latex-image>
<shortdescription>Natural deduction proof</shortdescription></image>
<image width="36%"><latex-image label="proof-9a3c793890">
$\begin{nd}
	\have[m]{ab}{\metaA{}\eor\metaB{}}
	\have[n]{na}{\enot\metaA{}}
	\have[\ ]{b}{\metaB{}} \oe{ab,na}
\end{nd}$
</latex-image>
<shortdescription>Natural deduction proof</shortdescription></image>
<p><alert>Conditional Introduction</alert></p>
<image width="35%"><latex-image label="proof-8907ea98cf">
$\begin{nd}
	\open
		\hypo[m]{a}{\metaA{}} \by{want \metaB{}}{}
		\have[n]{b}{\metaB{}}
	\close
	\have[\ ]{ab}{\metaA{}\eif\metaB{}}\ci{a-b}
\end{nd}$
</latex-image>
<shortdescription>Natural deduction proof</shortdescription></image>
<p><alert>Conditional Elimination</alert></p>
<image width="37%"><latex-image label="proof-e82d25bce0">
$\begin{nd}
	\have[m]{ab}{\metaA{}\eif\metaB{}}
	\have[n]{a}{\metaA{}}
	\have[\ ]{b}{\metaB{}} \ce{ab,a}
\end{nd}$
</latex-image>
<shortdescription>Natural deduction proof</shortdescription></image>
<p><alert>Biconditional Introduction</alert></p>
<image width="36%"><latex-image label="proof-938298bcf0-2">
$\begin{nd}
	\have[m]{ab}{\metaA{}\eif\metaB{}}
	\have[n]{ba}{\metaB{}\eif\metaA{}}
	\have[\ ]{c}{\metaA{}\eiff\metaB{}} \bi{ab, ba}
\end{nd}$
</latex-image>
<shortdescription>Natural deduction proof</shortdescription></image>
<p><alert>Biconditional Elimination</alert></p>
<image width="37%"><latex-image label="proof-ba91f4be28">
$\begin{nd}
	\have[m]{ab}{\metaA{}\eiff\metaB{}}
	\have[n]{a}{\metaB{}}
	\have[\ ]{b}{\metaA{}} \be{ab,a}
\end{nd}$
</latex-image>
<shortdescription>Natural deduction proof</shortdescription></image>
<image width="37%"><latex-image label="proof-34d89cbf39">
$\begin{nd}
	\have[m]{ab}{\metaA{}\eiff\metaB{}}
	\have[n]{a}{\metaA{}}
	\have[\ ]{b}{\metaB{}} \be{ab,a}
\end{nd}$
</latex-image>
<shortdescription>Natural deduction proof</shortdescription></image>
<p><alert>Negation Introduction</alert></p>
<image width="44%"><latex-image label="proof-8450bcd162">
$\begin{nd}
\open
	\hypo[m]{na}\metaA{}\by{for reductio}{}
	\have[n]{b}\metaB{}
	\have[o]{nb}{\enot\metaB{}}
\close
\have[\ ]{a}[\ ]{\enot\metaA{}}\ni{na-b, na-nb}
\end{nd}$
</latex-image>
<shortdescription>Natural deduction proof</shortdescription></image>
<p><alert>Negation Elimination</alert></p>
<image width="45%"><latex-image label="proof-8f262c7eb5">
$\begin{nd}
\open
	\hypo[m]{na}{\enot\metaA{}}\by{for reductio}{}
	\have[n]{b}\metaB{}
	\have[o]{nb}{\enot\metaB{}}
\close
\have[\ ]{a}[\ ]\metaA{}\ne{na-b, na-nb}
\end{nd}$
</latex-image>
<shortdescription>Natural deduction proof</shortdescription></image></subsection>
<subsection xml:id="quickreference-quantifier-rules-2">
<title>Quantifier Rules</title>
<p><alert>Existential Introduction</alert></p>
<image width="43%"><latex-image label="proof-1f5008902e">
$\begin{nd}
	\have[m]{a}{\metaA{}}
	\have[\ ]{c}{\exists \script{x}\metaA{}\substitutesome{\script{c}^\ast}{\script{x}}} \Ei{a}
\end{nd}$
</latex-image>
<shortdescription>Natural deduction proof</shortdescription></image>
<p><em>
<m>^\ast \script{x}</m> may replace some or all occurrences of <m>\script{c}</m>.</em></p>
<p><alert>Existential Elimination</alert></p>
<image width="50%"><latex-image label="proof-b8d1e140ef-2">
$\begin{nd}
	\have[m]{a}{\exists \script{x}\metaA{}}
	\open	
		\hypo[n]{b}{\metaA{}\substitute{\script{x}}{\script{c}^\ast}} \by{for $\exists${}E}{}
		\have[p]{c}{\metaB{}}
	\close
	\have[\ ]{d}{\metaB{}} \Ee{a,b-c}
\end{nd}$
</latex-image>
<shortdescription>Natural deduction proof</shortdescription></image>
<p><em>
<m>^\ast \script{c}</m> must not occur anywhere earlier in the proof or in <m>\metaB{}</m>.</em></p>
<p><alert>Universal Introduction</alert></p>
<image width="37%"><latex-image label="proof-67ff222333-2">
$\begin{nd}
	\have[m]{a}{\metaA{}\substitute{\script{x}}{\script{c}^\ast}}
	\have[\ ]{c}{\forall \script{x}\metaA{}} \Ai{a}
\end{nd}$
</latex-image>
<shortdescription>Natural deduction proof</shortdescription></image>
<p><em>
<m>^\ast \script{c}</m> must not occur in <m>\metaA{}</m> or in any undischarged assumption.</em></p>
<p><alert>Universal Elimination</alert></p>
<image width="37%"><latex-image label="proof-676255e474-2">
$\begin{nd}
	\have[m]{a}{\forall \script{x}\metaA{}}
	\have[\ ]{c}{\metaA{}\substitute{\script{x}}{\script{c}}} \Ae{a}
\end{nd}$
</latex-image>
<shortdescription>Natural deduction proof</shortdescription></image></subsection>
<subsection xml:id="quickreference-identity-rules-2">
<title>Identity Rules</title>
<p><alert>Identity Introduction</alert></p>
<image width="19%"><latex-image label="proof-2c10edc701">
$\begin{nd}
	\have[\ \,\,\,]{x}{\script{c}{=}\script{c}} \by{=I}{}
\end{nd}$
</latex-image>
<shortdescription>Natural deduction proof</shortdescription></image>
<p><alert>Identity Elimination</alert></p>
<image width="43%"><latex-image label="proof-2bcaee49bd-2">
$\begin{nd}
	\have[m]{e}{\script{c}{=}\script{d}}
	\have[n]{a}{\metaA{}}
	\have[\ ]{ea1}{\metaA{}\substitutesome{\script{c}}{\script{d}}} \by{=E}{e,a}
	\have[\ ]{ea2}{\metaA{}\substitutesome{\script{d}}{\script{c}}} \by{=E}{e,a}
\end{nd}$
</latex-image>
<shortdescription>Natural deduction proof</shortdescription></image>
<p><em>One name may replace some or all occurrences of the other.</em></p></subsection>
<subsection xml:id="quickreference-derived-rules">
<title>Derived Rules</title>
<p><alert>Reiteration</alert></p>
<image width="24%"><latex-image label="proof-19d39c643e">
$\begin{nd}
	\have[m]{a}{\metaA{}}
	\have[\ ]{c}{\metaA{}} \by{R}{a}
\end{nd}$
</latex-image>
<shortdescription>Natural deduction proof</shortdescription></image>
<p><alert>Dilemma</alert></p>
<image width="42%"><latex-image label="proof-77c95141aa">
$\begin{nd}
	\have[m]{ab}{\metaA{}\eor\metaB{}}
	\have[n]{ac}{\metaA{}\eif\metaC{}}
	\have[p]{bc}{\metaB{}\eif\metaC{}}
	\have[\ ]{a}{\metaC{}} \by{DIL}{ab,ac,bc}
\end{nd}$
</latex-image>
<shortdescription>Natural deduction proof</shortdescription></image>
<p><alert>Modus Tollens</alert></p>
<image width="37%"><latex-image label="proof-536da82d82-2">
$\begin{nd}
	\have[m]{ab}{\metaA{}\eif\metaB{}}
	\have[n]{a}{\enot\metaB{}}
	\have[\ ]{b}{\enot\metaA{}} \by{MT}{ab,a}
\end{nd}$
</latex-image>
<shortdescription>Natural deduction proof</shortdescription></image>
<p><alert>Hypothetical Syllogism</alert></p>
<image width="37%"><latex-image label="proof-1c0a6a3fbf-2">
$\begin{nd}
	\have[m]{ab}{\metaA{}\eif\metaB{}}
	\have[n]{bc}{\metaB{}\eif\metaC{}}
	\have[\ ]{ac}{\metaA{}\eif\metaC{}}\by{HS}{ab,bc}
\end{nd}$
</latex-image>
<shortdescription>Natural deduction proof</shortdescription></image></subsection>
<subsection xml:id="quickreference-replacement-rules">
<title>Replacement Rules</title>
<p><alert>Commutativity</alert> (Comm)</p>
<p><m>(\metaA{}\eand\metaB{}) \Longleftrightarrow (\metaB{}\eand\metaA{})</m></p>
<p><m>(\metaA{}\eor\metaB{}) \Longleftrightarrow (\metaB{}\eor\metaA{})</m></p>
<p><m>(\metaA{}\eiff\metaB{}) \Longleftrightarrow (\metaB{}\eiff\metaA{})</m></p>
<p><alert>DeMorgan</alert> (DeM)</p>
<p><m>\enot(\metaA{}\eor\metaB{}) \Longleftrightarrow (\enot\metaA{}\eand\enot\metaB{})</m></p>
<p><m>\enot(\metaA{}\eand\metaB{}) \Longleftrightarrow (\enot\metaA{}\eor\enot\metaB{})</m></p>
<p><alert>Double Negation</alert> (DN)</p>
<p><m>\enot\enot\metaA{} \Longleftrightarrow \metaA{}</m></p>
<p><alert>Material Conditional</alert> (MC)</p>
<p><m>(\metaA{}\eif\metaB{}) \Longleftrightarrow (\enot\metaA{}\eor\metaB{})</m></p>
<p><m>(\metaA{}\eor\metaB{}) \Longleftrightarrow (\enot\metaA{}\eif\metaB{})</m></p>
<p><alert>Biconditional Exchange</alert> (<m>\eiff</m>ex)</p>
<p><m>[(\metaA{}\eif\metaB{})\eand(\metaB{}\eif\metaA{})] \Longleftrightarrow (\metaA{}\eiff\metaB{})</m></p>
<p><alert>Quantifier Negation</alert> (QN)</p>
<p><m>\enot\forall\script{x}\metaA{} \Longleftrightarrow \exists\script{x}\enot\metaA{}</m></p>
<p><m>\enot\exists\script{x}\metaA{} \Longleftrightarrow \forall\script{x}\enot\metaA{}</m></p></subsection>
</section>
</appendix>
